{"availability":"available","full":"elegra1965-source/nms-galactic-map","name":"nms-galactic-map","description":"A fan-made 3D No Man's Sky galaxy map and portal address decoder","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":3,"forks":1,"created":"2026-08-04T13:20:32Z","updated":"2026-10-18T22:37:01Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://nms-galaxy-map.netlify.app","topics":["fan-project","galaxy-map","no-mans-sky","portal-address","procedural-generation","pwa","star-map","threejs","webgl"],"demo":"https://nms-galaxy-map.netlify.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T22:44:43.928Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T22:44:43.928Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T22:44:43.928Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T11:07:54.667Z","stars":2,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-11T14:52:56.419Z","stars":2,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-17T18:52:30.206Z","stars":3,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-18T22:44:43.928Z","stars":3,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A fan-made No Man's Sky tool built on one fact the game never spells out: a 12-glyph portal address is not an opaque code, it's a 3D coordinate. Decode it and you're not reading a string — you're pointing at an exact voxel in a 4096 x 256 x 4096 grid that spans the whole galaxy. So the portal decoder and the galaxy map are the same tool: type or tap an address, and you fly straight to that point, in three dimensions, in a browser.","Fan-made, built on public wiki data and reverse-engineered address maths. Not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Hello Games."],"features":["What can this map do?","How does a portal address become a 3D location?","What files make up this repo, and what's deliberately not in here?","What real No Man's Sky data does this use?","Can I import my own save file, and is it uploaded anywhere?"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elegra1965-source/nms-galactic-map/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d07a737c5942